<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms buy 23,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms buy 23,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd bought a combined 23,500 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat on Friday from Japanese trading house Mitsubishi Corp, company officials said.  </p>
<p>Cheiljedang bought 9,000 tonnes at basis prices over July futures on the U.S grain futures exchanges including the Chicago Board of Trade, they said. Dongah Flour purchased the remaining 14,500 tonnes at fixed rices.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for June 1-30 to the southeastern port of Pusan.</p>
